## Bezel vs Solitaire vs Halo vs Pavé for Marquise

A bezel is one of four main setting families for marquise. Quick comparison:

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Setting Family</th><th>Setting Cost</th><th>Tip Protection</th><th>Fire</th><th>Daily Wear</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Solitaire</strong></td><td>$790–$2,850</td><td>Depends on prongs</td><td>High</td><td>Depends on prong spec</td><td>Classic. See <a href="/marquise-solitaire-engagement-ring">solitaire guide</a>.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Halo</strong></td><td>$1,255–$5,985</td><td>High</td><td>Very High</td><td>Occasional catch</td><td>Bigger-looking. See <a href="/marquise-halo-engagement-ring">halo guide</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pavé</strong></td><td>$1,190–$4,850</td><td>Depends on centre prongs</td><td>Max</td><td>Pavé accents can drop</td><td>Fire-max. See <a href="/marquise-pave-engagement-ring">pavé guide</a>.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Bezel</strong></td><td>$990–$4,625</td><td>Total (full bezel)</td><td>Moderate</td><td>Zero catch risk</td><td>Our durability pick.</td></tr></tbody></table>

