## How to Verify a Marquise Bezel Before You Buy

Three checks every ring must pass before you commit.

**Check 1 — Confirm full bezel (not partial).** The 360° video should show the metal wall wrapping the whole stone girdle including both tips. If the tips show exposed stone edge, the setting is partial bezel — walk or re-spec at order.

**Check 2 — Confirm the bezel wall height is 1.0–1.5 mm.** The listing often states this. If not, ask the retailer. Walls under 1.0 mm are too thin for proper protection; walls over 1.5 mm catch on daily objects.

**Check 3 — Confirm the metal is platinum for lifetime wear OR accept the 14k gold lifespan limitation.** [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) and [GIA 4Cs](https://4cs.gia.edu/) both certify loose stones only — the setting metal is on the retailer's listing. Platinum is the correct answer for lifetime bezel; 14k gold needs re-tightening at year 15–20.

I run these three checks before I quote any client on a bezel ring. The bezel is the only setting style that mechanically eliminates marquise tip chip risk. All three checks must pass for the ring to deliver on that promise.

